id: pm-github-quay
title: Adopt SDK 2026.11.4 contracts while retaining atomic import rollback guarantees
description: "PR 194 now targets exact pm-cli 2026.11.4, pm-ops 2026.11.4 and pm-changelog 2026.10.31. GH-1614 literal identity normalization is fixed with real-SDK revert proof. The current compensation matrix is 1 passed and 2 failed: fresh refresh cleanup passes; source-lifecycle rollback after finalization and recovered refresh-plan cleanup remain blocked by GH-1591 transaction ownership. pm-cli#1656 must supply a supported journaled lifecycle finalizer. Preserve all rollback, peer-write safety and replay-plan assertions; never bypass ownership guards. Minimum consumer isolation is tracked by pm-github-gevp and issue 199."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[8]: ci,dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1656","gh:unbraind/pm-github#194","gh:unbraind/pm-github#197",migration,sdk,sdk-adoption
created_at: "2026-11-02T09:17:15.200Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T20:49:51.572Z"
assignee: codex-toolchain-1104
claim_principal: codex-toolchain-1104
author: pi-glm
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T09:27:51.980Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Reproduced the real-SDK compensation failure on the actual lockfile SDK 2026.10.28 (manifest remains >=2026.10.17). Root cause is the pm-cli 2026.10.26 GH-1591 ownership-proof hardening in src/sdk/item-transaction.ts. Before .26, compensateByRestore forced a timestamp restore. Since .26, hasOwnedCompensationEffects requires exclusive step ownership or a sibling compensation restoring the exact forward-state hash. commitGithubImportTransaction calls persistImportFidelity from its committing observer; that appends a separate import event (Preserve GitHub source lifecycle), so an ordinary subsequent observer failure correctly refuses rollback with transaction_partial_mutation rather than overwriting an unowned event. Classification: production integration depends on the former broad compensation behavior. Do not loosen the assertion or disable the SDK safety guard. Investigating a supported journaled finalizer; callback reordering or moving fidelity after commit would stop testing rollback after finalization and weaken the import guarantee."
  "2026-11-03T09:30:06.714Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Supported API review: BulkItemMutation accepts create/update/close/release, and onTransition is an observer, not a journaled custom mutation. Exact lifecycle timestamps currently require persistImportFidelity/mutateItem. No safe small production fix was found on the existing supported SDK range: post-commit finalization weakens rollback, callback reordering bypasses the failing boundary, and spoofed internal markers or force restoration bypass ownership safety. Added docs/atomic-finalization-sdk.md with versions, GH-1591 source comparison, minimal public SDK call shape, actual refusal and required journaled-finalizer support. Keep the existing regression red and report this as a production integration blocker with an upstream API requirement, not an asserted SDK regression. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-11-03T09:45:26.334Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Minimal public SDK reproducer verified on installed 2026.10.28: one bulk UPDATE, then client.update in committing, then an ordinary thrown error. Result is AggregateError compensation failed with transaction_partial_mutation; the item retains title Changed and description Source finalization, journal status compensating. This confirms the ownership-proof boundary independently of GitHub HTTP fixtures and source lifecycle timestamp handling. The synthetic tracker was removed after read-back. Typecheck and lint pass; npm test and the focused linked regression are running with the documented expected failure. Coverage/release gates were not run."
  "2026-11-03T10:04:00.584Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Final bounded gates: npm test ran build/build:test for about 34 minutes and reported 343 tests, 282 pass, zero assertion failures, 61 canceled when stopped before later files; this does not cover the known import-fidelity regression. The focused real-SDK import-fidelity regression explicitly fails with incomplete compensation, including through pm test. A separate minimal public SDK call reproduces the same transaction_partial_mutation and compensating journal. Typecheck, lint, privacy and changelog regeneration/check pass. Coverage and release:check were not run. Pushing documentation and complete diagnostic evidence only; the production finalizer integration remains blocked on a supported journaled raw lifecycle step. No assertions, ownership guards or production behavior were weakened. Coordinator should decide the upstream API request; no new upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-11-04T19:19:00.125Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Re-checking PR 194 after merging origin/main and adopting registry-confirmed pm-cli 2026.11.4, pm-ops 2026.11.4, pm-changelog 2026.10.31. Read issues 197 and 199 plus docs/atomic-finalization-sdk.md first. Preserve every compensation assertion and SDK ownership guard; verify the known failure on the current SDK before selecting a supported fix. Only focused tests run while the preceding package final coverage gate is active."
  "2026-11-04T19:23:09.230Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Root cause (production): pm-cli 2026.10.30 GH-1614 preserves typed assignee sentinel strings. normalizeImportValue erased none in assignment/sprint comparison, potentially hiding a real identity update as unchanged. New real-SDK identity regression fails 0/1 against the original source. Preserve literals, retain explicit absent/unset clears, and update exact unchanged-comparison assertions to distinguish empty and literal none values."
  "2026-11-04T19:25:15.713Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Current SDK recheck: the three existing focused compensation cases report 1 pass and 2 failures. Fresh refresh cleanup now passes; source-lifecycle rollback after finalization and recovered refresh-plan cleanup still fail with cannot safely compensate incomplete step. Classification: production integration relies on pre-GH-1591 broad rollback; the CLI ownership refusal is protective behavior, not an asserted upstream regression. Still needs pm-cli#1656 for a journaled owned lifecycle finalizer. SDK 2026.11.4 expected revision guards (GH-1576) do not extend the bulk mutation union or supply that ownership. Keep the remaining assertions unchanged."
  "2026-11-04T19:26:31.438Z",codex-toolchain-1104,Independent minimal public SDK recheck on 2026.11.4 confirms AggregateError with transaction_partial_mutation and retained compensating journal. One bulk update followed by client.update in committing and an ordinary thrown error leaves title Changed and description Source finalization instead of restoring Original. Documented exact remaining #1656 requirement without asserting the protective refusal itself is a CLI regression. Corrected sentinel/unchanged comparison tests pass 19/19.
  "2026-11-04T19:31:23.209Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Explicitly reverted only import-fidelity.ts to origin/main, confirmed the new real-SDK typed-identity test fails 0/1 (empty versus literal none), and restored the fix. Corrected focused identity/scheduled-refusal tests pass 19/19, and the linked sentinel test rerun passes. Typecheck and lint pass. Atomic lifecycle rollback and recovered refresh cleanup remain unchanged failing acceptance cases pending #1656."
  "2026-11-04T19:45:56.072Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Verified auxiliary gates on fix commit 065d3f8: typecheck, lint, privacy (8569 local objects), docstrings (28 files, 269 declarations), production dependency audit (zero vulnerabilities), changelog regeneration/check, and zero-duplication gate pass. dist is not tracked in this repository; built it for artifact acceptance. Only package.json/package-lock.json carry current development pins; current explanatory docs separate minimums from the independent pin and retain dated historical receipts. Full npm test will run serially after the preceding package coverage attempt ends."
  "2026-11-04T20:01:26.371Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Root cause (test): SDK 2026.10.30 GH-1614 rejects typed parent: none. Focused baselines: discussion-model 0/1, discussions 0/16, labels 3/13, label-import-model 0/3; the targeted 500-native-comma project writer also fails at its root fixture. Converted only those explicit resets to unset parent, merging it into existing unset lists. Existing hierarchy assignments, 500-sequence/native-tag models, preservation assertions and exact counts remain intact. Updated shared fixture, packed acceptance and manual validation companions consistently; the minimum-host probe now uses the portable explicit unset too."
  "2026-11-04T20:06:22.288Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"After fixture migration, the representative native discussion/label cases pass 2/2, build:test and lint pass, and the full exact-minimum consumer passes 1/1 again with explicit unset parent on SDK 2026.10.17. The longer focused 500-sequence batch was interrupted before completion to keep only one heavy suite active; it is not claimed passing. Full inventory remains queued for the serial npm test run."
  "2026-11-04T20:25:39.259Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Root cause (test): pm-changelog 2026.10.31 entry Fail closed when requested release notes have no matching section (pmc-pending-version-notes) now rejects an explicitly requested release that was suppressed as empty. changelog-placement.test.ts creates an intentionally empty September tag and requests that version while testing an October Unreleased delivery. Baseline is 3/5, with both tagged variants refusing MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE. Add the documented include-empty opt-in to that fixture caller script, retain every Unreleased/non-backfill assertion, and strengthen the tagged case to require exactly one visible empty historical section. No production workflow flags or guard semantics are changed."
  "2026-11-04T20:36:24.428Z",codex-toolchain-1104,The corrected changelog-placement file now passes 5/5 on Node 26.13.0. The intentionally empty September release is explicitly admitted with include-empty and asserted visible exactly once with the renderer empty body No changes.; October delivery remains Unreleased in both workflow variants. The full run had already loaded the prior fixture and records its two old failures; this focused receipt verifies their repair. Existing production workflow flags and every original placement/status/custom-script assertion are retained.
  "2026-11-04T20:41:27.014Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Additional test contract migration under pm-changelog 2026.10.31: closeout-workflow.test.ts had a flat caller generator receiving no-pending-release without all-release-tags. The documented historical-only exception requires both; otherwise an absent explicitly requested release is refused. Three focused workflow cases reproduced 0/3 with MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE, independently of the existing host/Git-advice note pm-github-gaq8. Add all-release-tags to that fixture caller only, preserving the malicious-content scan, zero-close cleanup, read-denial annotation and behavioral-revert assertions. Untagged placement already verifies the documented suppression, so no upstream regression is asserted."
  "2026-11-04T20:49:47.712Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"pm-changelog 2026.10.31 test contract: the workflow caller fixture requested historical-only notes via --no-pending-release without --all-release-tags. Three baseline privacy/zero-close/read-denial cases all failed with MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE before reaching their assertions. Match the documented historical-only exception by adding --all-release-tags to the fixture caller. Five focused cases now pass, including zero-close drift refusal and the staged-privacy behavioral revert; all assertions remain intact. This is separate from the older host-Git diagnosis and is not an established pm-cli regression."
